Z||000000||fieroX||11-04-2001||04:51 AM||||I decided that because I didnt have work today (well I guess yesterday now) that I would tear into my suspension and chop my springs.  I did alot of measuring first, so not to screw things up, and I think it turned out ok.  I started around 1:30 by 3 I had all four corners torn apart, by 4 my friend finally arrived with the spring compressor, by 6 I had the fronts done, (although I had a pretty major delay because of the lower control arm bushing not wanting to cooperate because of a bugered up thread, so that when I try to tighten the nut down it would spin the thing).<BR>I replaced the sway bar end links, and replaced the shocks with monroe sensitracs.  by 8 I had the rears cut and reassembled, and by 9 I had everything tightened and rolling.  I ended up cutting about 1.6 coils off the front, and 1.5 off the back.  this yeilded me about 1.5" drop in the front and 2 in the back.  It looks alot better, and it handles like its on rails.  I do have a weird shake now though.  It only happens during acceleration between 20 and 35 mph.  Im taking it in monday morning for a 4 wheel alignment, this should fix the problem.  I do have a slight camber problem on the front now, but I probably wont put more than a few miles on it until I can get it in to the shop.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Brian87egotrip||11-04-2001||08:12 AM||||I lowered mine, well a shop did it for me. I love it. Any pix's? I've always admired you do it yourselfers. Wish I had the automotive knowledge to be one. I am learning though.  <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
